WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:09.919
This video shows how to define the grade scale on your phone. The grade scale decides which letter grade and GPA a student gets for a percentage.

00:00:11.587 --> 00:00:21.787
Tap the menu button at the top left, open Academics, and then choose Grade Scale. Each grade is shown as a card with its percentage range and GPA.

00:00:24.001 --> 00:00:38.497
To add a higher grade, first make room for it. Tap Edit on grade A, change Max to 89.99, and tap Update. A message confirms the change, and the card now shows the new range.

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:49.186
Now tap Add Grade at the top of the page. A form opens with fields for the label, order, percentage range and GPA.

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:59.320
Type the grade label, here A plus. Then enter the minimum percentage 90, the maximum 100, and the grade point 4.5.

00:01:04.145 --> 00:01:13.481
Tap Create. A message confirms the grade, and the new A plus card appears in the list with its range from 90 to 100 percent.

00:01:16.485 --> 00:01:22.293
Your grade scale is ready. Results and report cards will now use it.
